!CHECK 220776.40 | 220335.50 00 | line 1 B,RODD -- a branch prints target+.10, so RODD is read to the HALF WORD only (220335.40); the tail of a vector whose head is on printed p.178
!CHECK 220777.00 | 220340.10 00 | line 2 B,RECC -- half-word only; RECC is DEFINED in the merged pp.99-176 body image at 220340.00 and this row agrees with it
!CHECK 220777.40 | 220342.10 00 | line 3 B,RNOECC -- half-word only; RNOECC is DEFINED in the merged body image at 220342.00 and this row agrees
!CHECK 221000.00 | 000014.47 04 | line 4 K MCP KVI,3,S FREE -- the 6-bit field is 2*index+1 (3 -> 7) plus 32 for a bit-32 operand, so this row reads S FREE's HALF WORD (12.32) and its index, nothing finer
!CHECK 221000.40 | 220715.32 C2 | line 5 BXE,K SOAR-.32 -- K SOAR is 220715.40, minus 32 bits is 220715.00; .32 is BXE's own modifier, not an address bit
!CHECK 221001.00 | 215003.02 B0 | line 6 V+,1,S BA MCP -- half-word only; S BA MCP is 215003.00 in the merged body image
!CHECK 221001.40 | 220715.50 00 | line 7 B,K SOAR -- the .50 is .40+.10, so this row DOES check K SOAR's half word
!CHECK 221002.00 | 010004.35 01 | line 8 Z IOD H LVI,14,S IOD I -- .35 is 2*14+1; S IOD I is half-word only (010004.00).  The comment "-INVALID IOD REF NO" is what settles the name's O and D
!CHECK 221002.40 | 217451.40 80 | line 9 SIC,S DISIC -- a SIC's half word carries the operand's FULL 24-bit bit address (Reference Manual printed p.41), so this is a BIT-EXACT reading of S DISIC at 217451.40.  Same card as line 10 (serial LA000119)
!CHECK 221003.00 | 217372.10 00 | line 10 B,S DISP -- half-word only; same card as line 9
!CHECK 221003.40 | 000032.26 30 | line 11 K UNA LV,11,$10 -- $10 is index register 10 at word 0o32; .26 is 2*11
!CHECK 221004.00 | 220726.50 00 | line 12 B,K NI -- .50 checks K NI's half word (220726.40)
!CHECK 221004.40 | 000010.00 80 | line 13 K NO GO BB,$L,K NOT AV, first half word -- $L is the accumulator left half at word 0o10 (C22-6531 Appendix A).  THIS LOCATION CARRIES THE PAGE'S FIRST LOCATION-COLUMN ASTERISK
!CHECK 221005.00 | 221066.34 02 | line 13 BB,$L,K NOT AV, second half word -- a BB branch address is 19 bits of HALF WORD, printed target+.34; byte 02 is mod=00 cond=1
!CHECK 221005.40 | 000002.07 04 | line 14 KVI,3,2.0 -- an immediate 2.0; .07 is 2*3+1 with no bit-32 term.  -IF $CCW, PROCEED
!CHECK 221006.00 | 220743.32 C2 | line 15 BXE,K OP OK -- half-word only (220743.00)
!CHECK 221006.40 | 000002.47 04 | line 16 KVI,3,2.32 -- .47 is 0o40+0o07, the 32 of "2.32" plus 2*3+1.  THIS ROW PROVES THE 6-BIT FIELD'S DECOMPOSITION, because both halves are written in the statement.  -IF $REL, PROCEED
!CHECK 221007.00 | 220735.32 C2 | line 17 BXE,K K NI -- a DIFFERENT symbol from K NI: 220735.00 against 220726.40.  The volume OCR indexes K K NI's defining card at 220735.00 on another page
!CHECK 221007.40 | 000014.07 04 | line 18 KVI,3,D CHEX -- D CHEX is 12.0; contrast line 4's S FREE at 12.32, same word, different half.  -IF $CHEX, PROCEED
!CHECK 221010.00 | 220743.32 C2 | line 19 BXE,K OP OK -- identical bits to line 15 and line 23
!CHECK 221010.40 | 000012.47 04 | line 20 KVI,3,D FREE -- D FREE is 10.32 in the BODY image; the pp.15-98 IPL assembly's D FREE is a different symbol with value 0.  -IF $FREE, PROCEED
!CHECK 221011.00 | 220735.32 C2 | line 21 BXE,K K NI -- identical bits to line 17
!CHECK 221011.40 | 000015.07 04 | line 22 KVI,3,DIODEF -- DIODEF is 13.0
!CHECK 221012.00 | 220743.32 C2 | line 23 BXE,K OPOK -- printed closed up here and spaced on lines 15/19; one symbol, identical bits all three times
!CHECK 221012.40 | 000000.33 8A | line 24 BZB,SMULTI($10),K CHOPN, first half word -- S MULTI is bit 0o33 = 27 with dds (BU,1); the low nibble A is index 10
!CHECK 221013.00 | 221041.34 00 | line 24 BZB second half word -- byte 00 is mod=00 cond=0 (branch on ZERO bit); KCHOPN half-word only at 221041.00, on printed p.180
!CHECK 221013.40 | 000000.63 8B | line 25 BZB,SMOUNT($11),KCHOPN, first half word -- S MOUNT is bit 0o63 = 51, index 11
!CHECK 221014.00 | 221041.34 00 | line 25 BZB second half word -- same target as line 24
!CHECK 221014.40 | 000001.34 80 | line 26 L(BU,26),$TC, first half word -- $TC is the Time Clock, word 1 bit 28 = 0o34 (C22-6531 Appendix A), so this row READS the system symbol's bit address
!CHECK 221015.00 | 032000.20 50 | line 26 L second half word -- the VFL op/length word for a 26-bit unsigned load
!CHECK 221015.40 | 000001.40 8C | line 27 -(BU,26),S RMTC($12), first half word -- S RMTC is 1.32 with dds (BU,26); index 12 is the C.  -COMPUTE TIME LAG
!CHECK 221016.00 | 032000.30 10 | line 27 subtract, second half word
!CHECK 221016.40 | 770000.00 80 | line 28 KI(BU,6),Z RMTCC, first half word -- an immediate is LEFT-JUSTIFIED in the 24-bit A24 field, so this reads only the TOP SIX BITS of Z RMTCC (111111); the symbol's own length and lower bits are UNOBSERVABLE here
!CHECK 221017.00 | 406000.21 10 | line 28 Connect-immediate, second half word -- independent of the operand's value (measured: the same bits with the SYN set to 0)
!CHECK 221017.40 | 221041.37 40 | line 29 BZAH,KCHOPN -- the ONLY B/BZ indicator spelling strap_asm accepts that produces these bits; AH is indicator 62 and the comment is "-BRANCH IF TIME NOT ELAPSED", which is what line 27's subtraction sets
!CHECK 221020.00 | 000001.77 8C | line 30 BB1,SRMIND($12),KCHOPN, first half word -- S RMIND is 1.63 = 0o177 within word 1, printed 000001.77.  THIS LOCATION CARRIES THE PAGE'S SECOND LOCATION-COLUMN ASTERISK
!CHECK 221020.40 | 221041.34 0E | line 30 BB1 second half word -- byte 0E is mod=0b11 (set the bit to ONE) cond=1, which is what distinguishes BB1 from BB (02) and BZB (00); the comment says "SET SWTCH"
!CHECK 221021.00 | 000010.56 3C | line 31 LV,7,SCREEL($12) -- S CREEL is 8.32, so .56 is 0o40 + 2*7; the byte's low nibble C is index 12
!CHECK 221021.40 | 000000.65 8B | line 32 BB,SIMNT($11),Z ID06, first half word -- S IMNT is bit 0o65 = 53
!CHECK 221022.00 | 221023.34 02 | line 32 BB second half word -- Z ID06 is this page's own line 34 at 221023.00, so this row is a SELF-CHECK of the page's counter
!CHECK 221022.40 | 000000.16 37 | line 33 LV,7,0.0($7) -- .16 is 2*7 with a zero operand; byte 37's low nibble is index 7.  -GET NEXT REEL SLOT ADDRESS
!CHECK 221023.00 | 000000.42 87 | line 34 Z ID06 LF,TRENME($7), first half word -- T RENME is 0.34 = 0o42 with dds (BU,30)
!CHECK 221023.40 | 036000.06 70 | line 34 LF second half word -- 0o36 = 30, the dds length.  -TEST IF REEL IS SCRATCH
!CHECK 221024.00 | 000027.20 30 | line 35 LV,8,$7 -- $7 is index register 7 at word 0o27; .20 is 2*8
!CHECK 221024.40 | 221063.34 C2 | line 36 BRZ,Z ID14 -- half-word only; Z ID14 is 221063.00 on printed p.180.  -BR. IF SCRATCH
!CHECK 221025.00 | 221064.56 B0 | line 37 V+,7,Z RENME -- .56 is 0o40 + 2*7, so Z RENME's HALF WORD is checked at 221064.40
!CHECK 221025.40 | 221030.17 30 | line 38 SV,7,Z ID 10 -- .17 is 2*7+1; Z ID 10 is this page's own line 42 at 221030.00, another self-check
!CHECK 221026.00 | 222015.00 80 | line 39 TI,2,KEXTAP,Z ID03, first half word -- a TRANSMIT's A1 is a 24-bit BIT address, so KEXTAP is read here to 222015.00 but the low bits are the transmit's own; treated as half-word only
!CHECK 221026.40 | 221055.04 A0 | line 39 TI second half word -- A2 is a 19-bit HALF-WORD address, Z ID03 at 221055.00, on printed p.180
!CHECK 221027.00 | 221030.37 01 | line 40 LVI,15,$+1.0 -- $ is 221027.00, so the value is 221030.00; .37 is 2*15+1.  A SELF-CHECK of the counter
!CHECK 221027.40 | 230567.50 00 | line 41 B,SA6IQS -- the .50 checks SA6IQS's half word at 230567.40.  -CONVERT REEL NAME
!CHECK 221030.00 | 000000.00+ | line 42 Z ID 10 VF,0.0 -- a VALUE FIELD prints magnitude then sign; the first parameter of the SA6IQS call on lines 40/41
!CHECK 221030.40 | 000005 | line 43 CF,5 -- an 18-bit COUNT field, printed as six bare octal digits
!CHECK 221031.00 | 221056.10+ | line 44 VF,Z ID 04 -- a VF deposits the value directly, so this is a BIT-EXACT reading of Z ID 04 at 221056.10, and the .10 is real: the volume OCR indexes its defining card on another page as an entry-mode DD landing mid-word
!CHECK 221031.40 | 000000.40 8B | line 45 Z ID09A BB,SOWNER($11),Z ID15, first half word -- S OWNER is bit 0o40 = 32
!CHECK 221032.00 | 221045.74 02 | line 45 BB second half word -- .74 is .34 + 0o40, so Z ID15 is at 221045.40, the ODD half of the same word Z ID09X occupies
!CHECK 221032.40 | 221060.17 01 | line 46 LVI,7,Z ID04A -- .17 is 2*7+1, so Z ID04A is half-word only at 221060.00
!CHECK 221033.00 | 221045.00 80 | line 47 SIC,Z ID09X -- BIT-EXACT: Z ID09X is 221045.00, which is also the value printed p.166's deck already SYNs.  Same card as line 48 (serial LA000156)
!CHECK 221033.40 | 221042.10 00 | line 48 B,Z ID09 -- half-word only; p.166's deck SYNs the same 221042.00.  THIS LOCATION CARRIES THE PAGE'S THIRD LOCATION-COLUMN ASTERISK.  -GET JOB NAME
!CHECK 221034.00 | 000000.32 88 | line 49 BB,TREPR($8),Z ID13, first half word -- T REPR is 0.26 = 0o32 with dds (BU,1); index 8
!CHECK 221034.40 | 221047.34 02 | line 49 BB second half word -- Z ID13 at 221047.00, on printed p.180.  -BR. IF REEL FILE PROTECTED
!CHECK 221035.00 | 000011.17 01 | line 50 Z ID08 LVI,7,9.0 -- 9 decimal is 0o11; .17 is 2*7+1
!CHECK 221035.40 | 221350.00 80 | line 51 Z ID07 SIC,KCONVR -- BIT-EXACT: KCONVR is 221350.00, which is the value the merged body image already holds.  Same card as line 52 (serial LA000159)
