!CHECK 221036.40 | 221053.00+ | line 53 VF,Z ID 02A -- BIT-EXACT: the parameter word of the KCONV call on lines 51/52, Z ID 02A at 221053.00
!CHECK 221037.00 | 215470.40 80 | line 54 SIC,S COMIC -- BIT-EXACT: S COMIC is 215470.40, the merged body image's value.  Same card as line 55 (serial LA000161)
!CHECK 221037.40 | 215470.10 00 | line 55 B,S COMM -- half-word only; S COMM is 215470.00, the EVEN half of the word S COMIC's odd half occupies
!CHECK 221040.00 | 221050.00 80 | line 56 ,Z ID01 -- A NULL OPERATION (C22-6531 printed p.7's null-field rule; strap_asm's note cites printed p.133 lines 44-45 as the same shape).  It emits the address-and-index half word every full-word format begins with, so the FULL 24-bit bit address is printed and Z ID01 is pinned to the bit at 221050.00.  LAST ROW OF THE PAGE, a HALF WORD, so THE COUNTER LEAVES AT 221040.40, which is what printed p.180 must print
